course: dictionary
lesson: 11313
title: Yen: money or a wish?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning to use. «Every country chooses its own money, called its currency: ... Japan the yen (¥)» shows that yen is money.
explain: Numbers can mislead you. «A Japanese sweet may cost 100 yen and still be cheap.» A big number does not mean a big price, because one yen is worth very little.
explain: The informal meaning is a strong wish. «A yen to travel» means a strong longing to travel. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence: a strong wish to travel makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Yen is the money of Japan, and its sign is ¥.
fact: One yen is worth very little, so prices in Japan can have big numbers.
fact: Yen is the same word in the singular and the plural: one yen, many yen.
fact: Informally, a yen is a strong wish or longing for something, as in a yen to travel.
fact: China uses the yuan, which also has the sign ¥, so check which country a money problem is about.
exercise: «A Japanese sweet may cost 100 yen and still be cheap.» What is the yen in this sentence? | A type of Japanese food | A kind of Japanese sweet | A map of Japan | *The money used in Japan
exercise: Maya has a yen to visit Japan. What does yen mean here? | *A strong wish or longing | A Japanese word for hello | Money she needs for the trip | A ticket to Japan
exercise: In a maths problem you change pounds into yen. What is the yen? | *The money used in Japan | A map of Japan | The money used in China | A kind of sweet
test: «Every country chooses its own money.» Which country uses the yen? | Canada | China | Ukraine | *Japan
test: Which sign is used for the yen? | *¥ | £ | € | ₴
exam: Ella reads «a big number on a price does not mean a big price» and asks what it tells her about yen | Big numbers always mean big prices | Yen is a very expensive money | *One yen is worth very little, so the numbers are big | Yen is a kind of sweet
